\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Lemma}
\title{Nondegeneracy is the unit-weight condition}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{The form #{q_x} of \ref{fdip-00PB} is nondegenerate exactly when
every weight at #{x} is a unit. Its rank is then the number of
edges leaving #{x}. Over an ordered field, the signature is the
sign pattern of those weights.}

\proof{
\p{Nondegeneracy means that #{v\mapsto B_x(v,\cdot)} is an
isomorphism from the fibre to its dual. On the edge basis this
map is diagonal, with entries the weights. A diagonal map of a
free module is an isomorphism exactly when every diagonal entry
is a unit, and the rank is then the number of those entries.
Over an ordered field a unit weight is positive or negative, and
the signature counts those two classes.}
}
